---@meta
-- Generated by rs3-api-types from https://developer.runescape.com/rs/ui/interactive_components/list.html;
-- regenerate it with ./gradlew generate rather than editing it.

---These components allow users to select between various options, supporting single or multiple selection, and can be
---displayed as either a regular list, or as a dropdown list. `ONSELECTIONCHANGED` event are then triggered for any
---selection changes.
---
---Custom Visuals: Using custom or plugin-provided sprites is supported, however the provided sprites used for the
---header and button must represent a spritesheet containing all of the potential states in a vertical layout using the
---following order - `default`, `mouseover`, `dropdown open`, `disabled`.
---@class ui.List : ui.Component
---@field numSelectedEntries integer (Read-only) How many entries are currently selected on this list.
---@field selectedEntries ui.ListEntry[] (Read-only) Array containing the entries selected on this list.
---@field entryHeight integer Height for each displayed entry in interface units.
---@field entryIconScale integer Scaling factor applied to icons for entries, where `1` represents `1%`. Defaults to `100`.
---@field dropdownButtonOffset integer Horizontal offset applied to this list's dropdown button. Only used by dropdown lists.
---@field dropdownButtonSize integer Dimensions used for the dropdown button. Only used by dropdown lists.
---@field dropdownMaxVisibleEntries integer How many entries can be displayed on the dropdown. Controls whether the list is displayed as a dropdown or not - if it's a non-zero value, the list is displayed as a dropdown.
---@field isDropdown boolean (Read-only) Whether the list is displayed as a dropdown.
---@field maxSelected integer Sets the maximum number of selected entries at any one time. Does not affect dropdowns. May deselect entries to ensure the current selection does not exceed the new limit.
---@field entries ui.ListEntry[] (Read-only) Array containing all entries on this list.
---@field contentMargin ui.Margin (Modifiable Contents) Offsets used to determine the inner content area for this component.
---@field headerMargin ui.Margin (Modifiable Contents) Offsets used to determine the inner content area for this component's dropdown header. Only used by dropdown lists.
---@field scrollbar ui.ScrollBar (Modifiable Contents) Scroll bar proprties used when vertical scrolling is required.
---@field entryText ui.TextData (Modifiable Contents) Text properties used when displaying entries for this list.
---@field entrySprite ui.SpriteData (Modifiable Contents) Sprite properties used for the background.
---@field buttonSprite ui.SpriteData (Modifiable Contents) Sprite properties used for the dropdown's button. Only used by dropdown lists.
---@field headerSprite ui.SpriteData (Modifiable Contents) Sprite properties used for the dropdown's header. Only used by dropdown lists.
ui.List = {}

---Creates a new list on the specified parent.
---
---Warning: Creating a component can fail if there's already a component on that parent with the same category ID and
---dynamic ID, or if those are omitted and the application is unable to generate a valid ID for the component.
---@param parent ui.ComponentCollection Parent component to create this list in.
---@param categoryID? integer Category ID used to identify this component. Defaults to the parent's category ID if not specified.
---@param dynamicID? integer Dynamic ID used to identify this component. Defaults to auto-incrementing from the parent's dynamic ID if not specified.
---@return ui.List # The newly created list. The caller must set its layout and visual information afterwards.
function ui.List.new(parent, categoryID, dynamicID) end

---Adds an entry to this list with the provided label and ID.
---
---Warning: Entry IDs are expected to be unique, if the provided ID is already used by another entry, this function will
---fail and return false.
---@param label string The text to display for this entry.
---@param id integer Unique value used to identify this entry.
---@return boolean # True if the entry was added successfully, false otherwise. This function can fail and return false due to the provided ID already existing.
function ui.List:Add(label, id) end

---Clears existing entries from the list and adds all entries in the provided container to the list, optionally
---selecting the one with the provided ID.
---
---Warning: Entry IDs are expected to be unique, if the provided ID is already used by another entry, this function will
---fail and return false.
---@param entries string[] Array of entry names to add to this list. Their respective IDs are autogenerated using an auto-incrementing integer.
---@param selectedID? integer ID for the entry to be selected afterwards. If this is an invalid ID or not specified, the first entry will be selected instead for lists that always require at least one selected entry (dropdowns for example).
---@return boolean # True if the provided entries were valid and were successfully added to the list, false otherwise. This function can fail and return false due to the provided ID already existing, or due to invalid/malformed data.
---@overload fun(self: ui.List, entriesMap: table<string, integer>, selectedID?: integer): boolean
function ui.List:SetEntries(entries, selectedID) end

---Removes all entries from this list.
function ui.List:Clear() end

---Deselects all currently selected entries in a multiple selection list (defined via the `maxSelected` property). Does
---nothing for single selection lists.
function ui.List:UnselectAll() end

---Sets whether or not the entry associated with the provided ID is enabled and can be selected.
---@param id integer Numeric value associated with the entry to modify.
---@param enabled boolean Whether or not the entry should be enabled and selectable.
---@return boolean # True if there was an entry corresponding to the provided ID, false otherwise.
function ui.List:SetEntryEnabled(id, enabled) end

---Sets whether or not the entry associated with the provided ID is visible to the user.
---@param id integer Numeric value associated with the entry to modify.
---@param visible boolean Whether or not the entry should be enabled visible to the user.
---@return boolean # True if there was an entry corresponding to the provided ID, false otherwise.
function ui.List:SetEntryVisible(id, visible) end

---Sets whether or not the entry associated with the provided ID is selected, and optionally triggers the corresponding
---`ONSELECTIONCHANGED` events.
---@param id integer Numeric value associated with the entry to modify.
---@param selected boolean Whether or not the entry should be selected.
---@param triggerEvents? boolean Whether or not to emit `ONSELECTIONCHANGED` events for this change. Defaults to false.
---@return boolean # True if there was an entry corresponding to the provided ID, false otherwise.
function ui.List:SetEntrySelected(id, selected, triggerEvents) end

---Sets the icon for the entry associated with the provided ID.
---@param id integer Numeric value associated with the entry to modify.
---@param spriteID integer Numeric ID associated with the sprite to use as an icon for this entry.
---@return boolean # True if there was an entry corresponding to the provided ID, false otherwise.
function ui.List:SetEntryIcon(id, spriteID) end

---Returns whether or not the entry associated with the provided ID is enabled and selectable.
---@param id integer Numeric value associated with the entry to access.
---@return boolean # True if there was an entry corresponding to the provided ID and it was enabled, false otherwise.
function ui.List:GetEntryEnabled(id) end

---Returns whether or not the entry associated with the provided ID is visible to the user.
---@param id integer Numeric value associated with the entry to access.
---@return boolean # True if there was an entry corresponding to the provided ID and it was visible, false otherwise.
function ui.List:GetEntryVisible(id) end

---Returns whether or not the entry associated with the provided ID is selected.
---@param id integer Numeric value associated with the entry to access.
---@return boolean # True if there was an entry corresponding to the provided ID and it was selected, false otherwise.
function ui.List:GetEntrySelected(id) end

---Returns whether or not there's an entry associated with the provided ID.
---@param id integer Numeric value associated with the entry to check.
---@return boolean # True if there is an entry corresponding to the provided ID, false otherwise.
function ui.List:HasEntry(id) end

---In most cases, entries must be modified through methods on the list itself, however you can also iterate through the
---list contents via the `entries` property, which returns a collection of entries. These are fairly limited and mostly
---provide an easy way to read the various properties for the various entries.
---@class ui.ListEntry
---@field text string The label for this entry.
---@field id integer (Read-only) The value for this entry.
---@field enabled boolean (Read-only) Whether this entry can be selected.
---@field visible boolean (Read-only) Whether this entry is currently hidden.
---@field selected boolean (Read-only) Whether this entry is currently selected.
